&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The parse is bounded (4 MiB per cell, a nesting depth of 1000, a million
nodes), so a notebook from anyone cannot make it run long or exhaust memory;
a cell over the limits fails with a message saying so.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Names.&lt;/strong&gt; An R cell joins the &lt;a href="https://go-notebook.github.io/docs/main/cells/"&gt;rules of cells&lt;/a&gt; and the dependency
graph. Its names follow R&amp;rsquo;s scoping at the top level of the environment the
cell runs in:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Construct&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;In the notebook&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;x &amp;lt;- v&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;x = v&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;v -&amp;gt; x&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;&amp;quot;x&amp;quot; &amp;lt;- v&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;defines &lt;code&gt;x&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;assign(&amp;quot;x&amp;quot;, v)&lt;/code&gt; with a literal name&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;defines &lt;code&gt;x&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;x$a &amp;lt;- v&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;x[i] &amp;lt;- v&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;names(x) &amp;lt;- v&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;defines &lt;code&gt;x&lt;/code&gt;, and reads the &lt;code&gt;x&lt;/code&gt; it modifies&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;for (i in s)&lt;/code&gt; at the top level&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;defines &lt;code&gt;i&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;f &amp;lt;- function(…) …&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;f = \(…) …&lt;/code&gt; at the top level&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;defines the function &lt;code&gt;f&lt;/code&gt;: it stays R&amp;rsquo;s&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;a free variable of the cell, or of a function&amp;rsquo;s body, that the cell does not assign&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;a use: the cell depends on the cell that defines it&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;the parameters and local assignments of a function, and what &lt;code&gt;local()&lt;/code&gt; assigns&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;stay inside it&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dynamic cells.&lt;/strong&gt; Some R cannot be analysed from its text: &lt;code&gt;x &amp;lt;&amp;lt;- v&lt;/code&gt;,
&lt;code&gt;assign&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;get&lt;/code&gt; with a computed name, &lt;code&gt;eval&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;parse&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;source&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;attach&lt;/code&gt;,
&lt;code&gt;library&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;require&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;environment&amp;lt;-&lt;/code&gt;. Such a cell is &lt;strong&gt;dynamic&lt;/strong&gt;: it depends
on every cell before it, and every later cell that reads a name depends on
it, so nothing it may define is missed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Across languages.&lt;/strong&gt; An R cell&amp;rsquo;s variables are seen by Go, Ruby and Julia
cells, and an R cell sees theirs, as between Ruby and Go (see
&lt;a href="https://go-notebook.github.io/docs/main/ruby/"&gt;Ruby cells&lt;/a&gt;); a function assigned at the top level stays in R. A
variable named like a Go keyword (&lt;code&gt;type&lt;/code&gt;) is not seen by Go cells.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id="what-does-not-work-yet-running"&gt;What does not work yet: running&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="what-does-not-work-yet-running"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#what-does-not-work-yet-running" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Running an R cell fails, clearly, and the cells that need it say why:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-code-block hx:relative hx:mt-6 hx:first:mt-0 hx:group/code"&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-markdown" data-lang="markdown"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;```go
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;n&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;10&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;```&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;```r
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;square&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;-&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;v&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;v^2&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;total&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;-&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;sum&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;square&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;seq_len&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;n&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)))&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;```&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;```go
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;total&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;```&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;```go
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;n&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;```&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class="hextra-code-copy-btn-container hx:opacity-0 hx:transition hx:group-hover/code:opacity-100 hx:flex hx:gap-1 hx:absolute hx:m-[11px] hx:right-0 hx:top-0"&gt;
&lt;button
class="hextra-code-copy-btn hx:group/copybtn hx:cursor-pointer hx:transition-all hx:active:opacity-50 hx:bg-primary-700/5 hx:border hx:border-black/5 hx:text-gray-600 hx:hover:text-gray-900 hx:rounded-md hx:p-1.5 hx:dark:bg-primary-300/10 hx:dark:border-white/10 hx:dark:text-gray-400 hx:dark:hover:text-gray-50"
title="Copy code"
aria-label="Copy code"
data-copied-label="Copied!"
&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-copy-icon hx:group-[.copied]/copybtn:hidden hx:pointer-events-none hx:h-4 hx:w-4"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-success-icon hx:hidden hx:group-[.copied]/copybtn:block hx:pointer-events-none hx:h-4 hx:w-4"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-code-block hx:relative hx:mt-6 hx:first:mt-0 hx:group/code"&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-console" data-lang="console"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="gp"&gt;$&lt;/span&gt; notebook run r.md
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="go"&gt;── cell 0 (line 4, ran in 11µs)
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="go"&gt;── cell 1 (line 8, not run)
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="go"&gt; error: R cells are parsed and checked, but not run yet: execution arrives with go-embedded-r&amp;#39;s evaluator (milestones M2 and M3)
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="go"&gt;── cell 2 (line 13, not run)
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="go"&gt; error: blocked: it depends on cell 1, an R cell, and R cells are not run yet
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="go"&gt;── cell 3 (line 17, ran in 24µs)
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="go"&gt; 20
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="go"&gt;notebook: 2 cell(s) failed
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class="hextra-code-copy-btn-container hx:opacity-0 hx:transition hx:group-hover/code:opacity-100 hx:flex hx:gap-1 hx:absolute hx:m-[11px] hx:right-0 hx:top-0"&gt;
&lt;button
class="hextra-code-copy-btn hx:group/copybtn hx:cursor-pointer hx:transition-all hx:active:opacity-50 hx:bg-primary-700/5 hx:border hx:border-black/5 hx:text-gray-600 hx:hover:text-gray-900 hx:rounded-md hx:p-1.5 hx:dark:bg-primary-300/10 hx:dark:border-white/10 hx:dark:text-gray-400 hx:dark:hover:text-gray-50"
title="Copy code"
aria-label="Copy code"
data-copied-label="Copied!"
&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-copy-icon hx:group-[.copied]/copybtn:hidden hx:pointer-events-none hx:h-4 hx:w-4"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-success-icon hx:hidden hx:group-[.copied]/copybtn:block hx:pointer-events-none hx:h-4 hx:w-4"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;(Real transcripts, from go-notebook v0.8.0.)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;an R cell never runs, and &lt;code&gt;notebook run&lt;/code&gt; exits non-zero;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;every cell that reads what an R cell defines, directly or through other
cells, in any language, is &lt;strong&gt;blocked&lt;/strong&gt;, not silently skipped;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;the other cells run as usual.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;go-notebook starts no external &lt;code&gt;R&lt;/code&gt;: the cells will run on go-embedded-r&amp;rsquo;s own
evaluator when it exists. The HTML page shows an R cell&amp;rsquo;s source uncoloured
(go-rouge has no R lexer).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id="in-the-browser"&gt;In the browser&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="in-the-browser"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#in-the-browser" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;The &lt;a href="https://go-notebook.github.io/playground/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;playground&lt;/a&gt; (v0.9.0 and later)
parses and checks R cells in the same way, in WebAssembly: the + menu and the
cell&amp;rsquo;s language menu offer R, its badge reads &lt;strong&gt;R · not runnable yet&lt;/strong&gt;, a
syntax error is shown at its line in R&amp;rsquo;s words, and the cells that read it
are blocked, in the page&amp;rsquo;s neutral style and not as failures.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The playground&amp;rsquo;s R example notebook (&lt;code&gt;#5-r&lt;/code&gt;) has an R cell, a Go cell blocked
on it and a Go cell that runs alone.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>